<title>FRANCE: French navy buys Thomson-CSF missiles.</title>
<headline>French navy buys Thomson-CSF missiles.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson-CSF unit Thomson-CSF Airsys said the French navy had purchased a substantial number of its VT1 missiles but said the navy refused to let it disclose the number or the value of the contract.</p>
<p>The missiles are to be used to equip the navy's Crotale air defence system on the new La Fayette-class of stealth frigates. The VT1 had a speed of Mach 3.5 and a range of 11 kms (6.6 miles), Thomson-CSF said in a statement.</p>
<p>They are intended to help the stealth frigates intercept highly-manoeuvrable sea-skimming anti-ship missiles.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
